IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc8-part8-organs-suicide`

-- ccc8-tests-part8-organs-suicide.l4 -- tests for ccc8-part8-organs-suicide.l4 (sections 240.1, 241, 242, 243). Expected values are written by hand from the text.
-- The stand-in below is NOT the penalty of section 787(1) (outside this part): it states nothing, so only the limb of this part is tested.
`s 242 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 240.1 -- trafficking in human organs`

-- (1) "Everyone commits an offence who (a) obtains an organ ..., knowing that the person from whom it was removed ... did not give informed consent to the removal, or being reckless as to whether or not such consent was given; (b) carries out, participates in or facilitates the removal ...; or (c) does anything in connection with the removal ..."
--                                                                                         knows reckless
#ASSERT `s 240.1(1) the person commits the offence of an organ removal without informed consent` `s 240.1(1)(a) obtains an organ to be transplanted into their body or into the body of another person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 240.1(1) the person commits the offence of an organ removal without informed consent` `s 240.1(1)(b) carries out, participates in or facilitates the removal of an organ from the body of another person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 240.1(1) the person commits the offence of an organ removal without informed consent` `s 240.1(1)(c) does anything in connection with the removal of an organ from the body of another person on behalf of, at the direction of or in association with the person who removes the organ` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 240.1(1) the person commits the offence of an organ removal without informed consent` `s 240.1(1)(a) obtains an organ to be transplanted into their body or into the body of another person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 240.1(1) the person commits the offence of an organ removal without informed consent` `s 240.1(1)(c) does anything in connection with the removal of an organ from the body of another person on behalf of, at the direction of or in association with the person who removes the organ` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) "Everyone commits an offence who obtains or participates in or facilitates the obtaining of an organ ..., knowing that it was obtained for consideration or being reckless as to whether or not it was obtained for consideration"
#ASSERT `s 240.1(2) the person commits the offence of obtaining an organ for consideration` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 240.1(2) the person commits the offence of obtaining an organ for consideration` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 240.1(2) the person commits the offence of obtaining an organ for consideration` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 240.1(2) the person commits the offence of obtaining an organ for consideration` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "Everyone who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years"
#ASSERT `s 240.1(3) the person commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 240.1(3) the person commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 240.1(3) the person commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 240.1(3) the person commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 240.1(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `s 240.1(3) the punishment` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 14, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

§ `Section 241 -- counselling or aiding suicide`

-- (7) "medical assistance in dying, medical practitioner, nurse practitioner and pharmacist have the same meanings as in section 241.1"
#ASSERT `s 241(7) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 241(7) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 241(7) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6) "the exemption set out in any of subsections (2) to (5) applies even if the person invoking the exemption has a reasonable but mistaken belief about any fact that is an element of the exemption"
#ASSERT `s 241(6) the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 241(6) the exemption applies despite a reasonable but mistaken belief` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) "Everyone is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years who, whether suicide ensues or not, (a) counsels a person to die by suicide or abets a person in dying by suicide; or (b) aids a person to die by suicide"
#ASSERT `s 241(1) the person commits the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 241(1) the person commits the offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 241(1) the person commits the offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 241(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `s 241(1) the punishment` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 14, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
-- (2) "No medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2"
--                                                                        practitioner  provides MAID  in accordance  (6)
#ASSERT `s 241(2) the practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE  NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 241(2) the practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 241(2) the practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 241(2) the practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 241(2) the practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "No person is a party to an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they do anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide a person with medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2"
#ASSERT `s 241(3) the person is a party to an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 241(3) the person is a party to an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 241(3) the person is a party to an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 241(3) the person is a party to an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) "No pharmacist who dispenses a substance to a person other than a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if the pharmacist dispenses the substance further to a prescription that is written by such a practitioner in providing medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2"
--                                                                        pharmacist   dispenses other  further to prescription (6)
#ASSERT `s 241(4) the pharmacist commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE  NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 241(4) the pharmacist commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 241(4) the pharmacist commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 241(4) the pharmacist commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 241(4) the pharmacist commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5) "No person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b) if they do anything, at another person's explicit request, for the purpose of aiding that other person to self-administer a substance that has been prescribed ... in accordance with section 241.2"
#ASSERT `s 241(5) the person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 241(5) the person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 241(5) the person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 241(5) the person commits an offence under paragraph (1)(b)` FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5.1) "For greater certainty, no social worker, psychologist, psychiatrist, therapist, medical practitioner, nurse practitioner or other health care professional commits an offence if they provide information to a person on the lawful provision of medical assistance in dying"
#ASSERT `s 241(5.1) the health care professional commits an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 241(5.1) the health care professional commits an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 241(5.1) the health care professional commits an offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 242 and 243`

-- 242 "A female person who, being pregnant and about to be delivered, with intent that the child shall not live or with intent to conceal the birth of the child, fails to make provision for reasonable assistance in respect of her delivery is, if the child is permanently injured as a result of the failure or dies immediately before, during or in a short time after birth, as a result of the failure, guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... five years; or (b) summary conviction"
--                                                                                        female pregnant intent(live) intent(conceal) fails injured dies
#ASSERT `s 242 the female person commits the offence of neglecting to obtain assistance in childbirth` TRUE TRUE TRUE  FALSE TRUE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 242 the female person commits the offence of neglecting to obtain assistance in childbirth` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE  TRUE FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 242 the female person commits the offence of neglecting to obtain assistance in childbirth` TRUE TRUE TRUE  FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 242 the female person commits the offence of neglecting to obtain assistance in childbirth` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 242 the female person commits the offence of neglecting to obtain assistance in childbirth` TRUE TRUE TRUE  FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 242 the female person commits the offence of neglecting to obtain assistance in childbirth` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 242 the female person commits the offence of neglecting to obtain assistance in childbirth` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 242 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 242 the punishment` `s 242 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 242 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
-- 243 "Every person who in any manner disposes of the dead body of a child, with intent to conceal the fact that its mother has been delivered of it, whether the child died before, during or after birth, is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... two years; or (b) summary conviction"
#ASSERT `s 243 the person commits the offence of concealing the body of a child` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 243 the person commits the offence of concealing the body of a child` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 243 the person commits the offence of concealing the body of a child` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 243 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 243 the punishment` `s 242 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty` EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, FALSE), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 242 test fixture: a stand-in for the section 787(1) penalty`
